  "rules": {
    "C": "C(arm) = median over cells of dM_main - dM_round",
    "S": "S(arm) = #cells where the donor-new-source patch is JOINT and the donor-ROUND-source patch of the same arm is not (target host new)",
    "SPEC": "SPEC iff dM_main > dM_round in >= 75% of cells AND in a majority of cells for >= 10 of 14 donor groups",
    "SUF": "SUF(arm) iff S(arm) >= 1/2 S(full) and SPEC(arm)",
    "always_reported": "S, SPEC, J_main, J_round, median dM and C per arm; per host; leave-one-donor-group-out of every verdict; energy shares, factors, capped shares; the S of each random frame, pooled and per host; change norm of every arm relative to full",
    "consistency_gate": "full = the M3 all-heads patch: its 208 rows equal M3's bitwise and S(full) = 51; meanD_host = the M6 pooled-donor arm: its 208 rows equal M6's bitwise and S = 39 (GPU, checked in the run); cs1 / chR_sm / cpar16_sm / cperp16_sm / cpos29 / cpos30 / sh2930 / sh0_28 = the M10 arms (same patch fields): their 8 x 208 rows equal M10's bitwise and S = 39 / 0 / 27 / 39 / 39 / 3 / 0 / 13; otherwise every verdict is INCONSISTENT_WITH_M3_M6_M10 and no claim",
    "interpretation_fixed_in_advance": "A pure amplitude threshold (A573) predicts SUF(cpos30_n29); AMPLITUDE_ONLY_EXCLUDED means c at position 30, given the size c has at 29, does not act, so the M10 P29 effect is not size alone. This separates position and direction together from size, not position from direction (c's direction at 30 differs from that at 29). AMPLITUDE_DRIVEN: the M10 P29 verdict reflects size. SHIFT_LOCAL_AT_TOTAL_NORM: with the same total shift norm, the shift at 29-30 alone suffices, so M10's SHIFT_NEEDS_ALL_POSITIONS was an amount effect; SHIFT_NEEDS_CONTEXT_POSITIONS: even the norm-matched local shift fails, so the shift must reach the context positions. SPLIT_BY_HOST: per responsive host, whether the part of c outside (or inside) the 16-dim common subspace repairs more cells than any of 10 contrast-sized random frames. All M11 arms except full are pooled-donor arms (effectively 8 host replicates, 3 responding in M9-M10); per-host S is the honest unit",
    "position_dose": "POS29_SMIN = the smallest s in 0.25, 0.5, 1 with SUF (cpos29_s025, cpos29_s05, cpos29); POS30_SMIN = the smallest s in 1, 2, 4 with SUF (cpos30, cpos30_s2, cpos30_s4); NONE if no s; the per-row norm ratio ||c_29|| / ||c_30|| is reported",
    "position_sm_verdict": "c kept at one span position and rescaled per row to the norm c has at the other position (cap 10): POSITION29_SPECIFIC iff SUF(cpos29_n30) and not SUF(cpos30_n29); AMPLITUDE_DRIVEN iff SUF(cpos30_n29) and not SUF(cpos29_n30); BOTH_POSITIONS_ACT_AT_SWAPPED_NORM iff both; P30_INERT_AT_P29_NORM iff neither. AMPLITUDE_ONLY_EXCLUDED iff not SUF(cpos30_n29)",
    "readouts": "M = conflict margin; A = logit(reject_conflict) - max(accept, wait); JOINT = M > 0 and A > 0; dM = M(patch) - M(in-run capture of host new)",
    "shift_dose": "SHIFT2930_UMIN = the smallest u in 1, 2, 4 with SUF (sh2930, sh2930_u2, sh2930_u4), or NONE; the per-row total and per-token norm ratios of the shift at 29-30 vs 0-28 and the applied factors are reported",
    "shift_sm_verdict": "the common shift (t = 1) only at span positions 29-30, rescaled per row so that its total norm equals that of the shift at 0-28 (sh2930_tm) or its per-token norm equals the mean per-token norm at 0-28 (sh2930_pt), cap 10, with the full c: SHIFT_LOCAL_AT_TOTAL_NORM iff SUF(sh2930_tm) and not SUF(sh2930_pt); SHIFT_LOCAL_AT_TOKEN_NORM iff the reverse; SHIFT_LOCAL_SUFFICES iff both; SHIFT_NEEDS_CONTEXT_POSITIONS iff neither",
    "size_gate": "rescaled rows: where not capped, the rescaled part has the target norm within 1e-3 relative (fail-closed in the runner): the kept position's c (target ||c|| at the other position), the shift at 29-30 (target the total or per-token-scaled norm at 0-28, or u times its own norm); the factors, the capped share and the pre-rescale shares are recorded",
    "split_by_host": "responsive host = a host where S(cs1) on its cells exceeds half its cells. Per responsive host: null_max = the maximum over the 10 random frames (crand16_sm and crand16_sm_s1 .. s4 from the pinned M10 raw, crand16_sm_s5 .. s9 here) of the host's S; OUTSIDE iff S(cperp16_sm) > null_max and S(cpar16_sm) <= null_max; INSIDE iff the reverse; BOTH iff both exceed; NEITHER iff neither. Verdict SPLIT_BY_HOST:<host8>=<v>,... over the responsive hosts",
    "split_null10": "SPLIT_NULL10 holds iff the median pooled S over the 10 random frames is <= 5 and none is SPEC; the pooled subspace verdict is re-applied with the M9 / M10 categories and the _UNRESOLVED suffix iff SPLIT_NULL10 fails",
    "units": "the 104 cross-group cells of M1-M6; cells share donors and hosts, and the pooled-mean arms vary with the donor only through the pool exclusion (effectively 8 hosts), so counts are descriptive decision rules, not independent tests; per-host S is always reported"
  },
